3582   E442             
3583   E442             ;This is unused in the macros. You must call it directly at $F1D5
3584   E442             ;The behavior of this command is probably the most complex. It 
3585   E442             ;starts at the last lamp in the range. If it is already set, then
3586   E442             ;the routine simply exits. If the last lamp is not set, the routine
3587   E442             ;goes down through each lamp in the range. If if finds a lamp on,
3588   E442             ;then it turns off that lamp, then goes back up to the next lamp
3589   E442             ;and turns it on. If no lamps are on in the range, then the first
3590   E442             ;lamp in the range is turned on.
3591   E442             ;The best example of this routine is for the 10-20-30 lamps on 
3592   E442             ;Jungle Lord. It will simply incrment the 10-20-30 lamps sequentially
3593   E442             ;and then stop at 30. If none are on, then it will turn on 10.
3594   E442 8D 4F       lampm_g         bsr     lampr_end               ;A = Last Lamp Level, B = Last Lamp BitPos
