5805   F0E5             ;**********************************************************************************
5806   F0E5             ;* NMI Routines - This section of code is run only when the 
5807   F0E5             ;*                diagnostic switch on the CPU board is pressed.
5808   F0E5             ;*                It will test the hardware and report any errors
5809   F0E5             ;*                via the LED display on the CPU board. If all tests
5810   F0E5             ;*                are passed, the LED display will show '0' and
5811   F0E5             ;*                the code jumps to the normal power-up routines.
5812   F0E5             ;*
5813   F0E5             ;* Errors are as Follows:
5814   F0E5             ;*
5815   F0E5             ;*      0 - Test Passed
5816   F0E5             ;*      1 - IC13 RAM Fault (Most Significant Nybble)
5817   F0E5             ;*      2 - IC16 RAM Fault (Least Significant Nybble)
5818   F0E5             ;*      3 - IC17 ROM 2 Fault (Location $F000-$FFFF)
5819   F0E5             ;*      4 - IC14 ROM 1 Fault (Location $E000-$EFFF)
5820   F0E5             ;*      5 - IC20 ROM 0 Fault (Location $D000-$DFFF)
5821   F0E5             ;*      6 - Not Used
5822   F0E5             ;*      7 - Not Used
5823   F0E5             ;*      8 - IC19 CMOS RAM Fault or Memory Protect Failure
5824   F0E5             ;*      9 - Coin Door Closed or Memory Protect Failure or IC19 CMOS RAM Fault
5825   F0E5             ;**********************************************************************************
